{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793637707,"nonce":"wvS4Xx7acgSilkQk04gg4bKD3C8=","title":"Canvas paths paint over later siblings in the same layer","message":"A canvas's fill_path/stroke_path output lands above elements that come after it in the tree and share its render layer, including their text: z-index on the later element does not help. Seen with cn::bar_chart, whose tooltip (a sibling after the canvas) was hidden behind a horizontal bar; the chart lifts its tooltip with .foreground() to work round it.\n\nExpected: paint follows tree order (and z-index) within a layer, as for any other element. Reproducer: a plot div holding canvas(..) drawing a filled path, then an absolute div with a background and text over the same area; the path covers the div.","files":null}]}